{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1783831998,"nonce":"H6l41N8+X1MG6S0DpwqwyED0i3s=","title":"[slice-4] engine: Gate step kind (durable suspend)","message":"Goal: approvals/timers/events at near-zero cost.\nA Gate built-in step kind suspends the run durably (RunStatus::Suspended) awaiting human approval, a timer, or an external event; release resumes the DAG. Survives deploys (version tolerance).\nAcceptance (real Postgres): a gated run suspends, persists across a scheduler restart, and resumes exactly once on approval.\nADRs: 0008, 0011, 0022.","files":null}]}